  "slug": "wine-fondue",
  "name": "Wine Fondue",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "A lovely wine fondue for cooking chicken, rabbit or veal. Dip bite-size pieces of raw meat into the boiling fondue until cooked.",
  "cuisine": "Swiss",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Pour wine into a saucepan, and season with cinnamon stick, coriander, pepper, cloves, sugar, salt, celery salt, and garlic salt. Let sit for 1 hour, then bring to a boil. Filter through a fine sieve or colander lined with cheesecloth, and transfer to the fondue pan. Bring to a boil before using."
    }
  ],
